node.doctext:
I have a file parser that reads a configuration file that defines what the record separator is. Something like this:
<p>
Config file
</p>
<p>
RECORDSEPARATOR=\r\n
</p>
<code>
#!/usr/bin/perl
use strict;
# read configuration parameters into hash

my $recordseparator = $CFG{'RECORDSEPARATOR'};
if (defined $recordseparator && $recordseparator ne '') {
   $/ = $recordseparator;
   print STDOUT ":$/:"; # for test
}
else {
  $/ = "\n";
}
</code>


The above code interprets to $/ = '\r\n' instead of $/ = "\r\n"  
I know I've done something similar in the past but for the life of me I can't figure this out.
